  {
   "id": "title",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1500,
   "y": -980,
   "width": 900,
   "height": 120,
   "text": "# Minideck \u2014 every wire\n47 wires \u00b7 generated from the wiring plan (`python3 wiring_canvas.py`)"
  },
  {
   "id": "legend",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -560,
   "y": -980,
   "width": 320,
   "height": 294,
   "text": "**Wire colours**\n- <span style=\"color:#e03131\">\u25a0</span> 5 V / battery +\n- <span style=\"color:#868e96\">\u25a0</span> GND\n- <span style=\"color:#f08c00\">\u25a0</span> 3.3 V\n- <span style=\"color:#1c7ed6\">\u25a0</span> I\u00b2C\n- <span style=\"color:#2f9e44\">\u25a0</span> I\u00b2S audio\n- <span style=\"color:#f2c94c\">\u25a0</span> UART\n- <span style=\"color:#e9ecef\">\u25a0</span> GPIO\n- <span style=\"color:#9c36b5\">\u25a0</span> USB (SDR)\n- <span style=\"color:#c46b2c\">\u25a0</span> HDMI ribbon\n- <span style=\"color:#a5b4c8\">\u25a0</span> antenna coax"
  },
  {
   "id": "notes",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -200,
   "y": -980,
   "width": 720,
   "height": 164,
   "text": "**Notes**\n- Pin 1 is at the Radxa's microSD end (its left end in the case): check the square pad before soldering.\n- One wire per Radxa pad; the CardKB is chained onto the PN532's I\u00b2C pins.\n- SDR: USB over header pins 27/28 after swapping R32/R39 \u2192 R45/R46 on the Radxa.\n- Gauges: 22\u201324 AWG for power, 28\u201330 AWG for signals, 1.13 mm u.FL coax for antennas."
  }
 ],
